1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Flappy Bird is a single-button arcade game where the player controls a bird 
that must fly through a series of moving pipes without colliding with them. 
The game increases in difficulty over time by speeding up and shrinking the 
gap between pipes. A bonus coin system rewards skilled players with extra 
points.

GAME GENRE     : Arcade / Endless Runner
CONTROL SCHEME : Single Button (Tap to Flap/Jump)
DIFFICULTY     : Progressive (increases every 5 points)
DISPLAY        : 128x64 OLED (SH1106 driver, SPI interface)
MICROCONTROLLER: Arduino Nano

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO PLAY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Power on the device - Start Screen appears showing "FLAPPY BIRD"
2. Press the button to begin the game
3. Tap the button repeatedly to make the bird "flap" upward
4. Gravity constantly pulls the bird down - timing your taps controls altitude
5. Navigate through the gaps between pipes without touching them
6. Collect bonus coins (small circles) for +3 extra points
7. Colliding with a pipe or screen edge ends the game
8. Press the button again on the Game Over screen to restart

