--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WIRING / PIN CONNECTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OLED DISPLAY (SPI MODE):
    OLED Pin        Arduino Nano Pin
    -----------------------------------
    MOSI (SDA)  ->  D10
    CLK (SCK)   ->  D8
    DC          ->  D7
    CS          ->  D5
    RST         ->  D9
    VCC         ->  5V (or 3.3V depending on your module)
    GND         ->  GND

PUSH BUTTON:
    Button Pin 1  ->  D2 (Arduino)
    Button Pin 2  ->  GND
    
    NOTE: Code uses INPUT_PULLUP mode, meaning the pin is internally 
    pulled HIGH. When the button is pressed (connecting pin to GND), 
    the reading changes. 
    
    IMPORTANT: In this code, digitalRead(buttonPin) == HIGH is used 
    to detect a "pressed" state. Depending on your specific button 
    wiring (Normally Open vs Normally Closed), you may need to change 
    this comparison to LOW instead. This is noted directly in the code 
    comments at each digitalRead() call.

POWER:
    4x AA Battery Pack (6V) -> Arduino Nano VIN pin, GND -> GND
    (Alternative: USB power during development/testing)

