5. FUNCTION-BY-FUNCTION BREAKDOWN
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.1 void setup()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Runs once at power-on. Initializes hardware and starting game state.

WHAT IT DOES:
  1. Sets buttonPin as INPUT_PULLUP (internal resistor enabled, pin reads 
     HIGH by default, changes when button pressed)
  2. Initializes the OLED display (display.begin(0, true))
  3. Clears the display buffer and pushes a blank screen
  4. Seeds the random number generator using noise from analog pin A0 
     (ensures different pipe patterns each power-on)
  5. Initializes the 3 pipes:
     - Spaced 50 pixels apart horizontally (pipeX[i] = 128 + i * 50)
     - Random initial gap position (between Y=10 and Y=44)
     - Random initial movement direction for the "moving gap" effect

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.2 void loop()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Main game state machine. Runs continuously, forever.

LOGIC FLOW:
  IF game has not started:
      -> Show start screen
      -> Check for button press to begin game
  ELSE IF game is running (not game over):
      -> Update game logic (physics, collisions, scoring)
      -> Draw current frame
      -> Wait 30ms (controls game speed/framerate)
  ELSE (game over):
      -> Show game over screen with final score
      -> Check for button press to reset and play again

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.3 void drawBird(int x, int y)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Draws the bird character at given coordinates using layered shapes.

VISUAL BREAKDOWN:
  - Body : A filled circle, radius 3px, centered at (x, y)
  - Beak : A small filled triangle pointing right (in front of the body)
  - Eye  : A tiny filled circle drawn in BLACK on top of the body (creates 
           a "cutout" effect since OLED is monochrome)
  - Wing : An animated triangle that alternates between two positions 
           based on the flapFrame boolean, creating a simple flapping 
           animation effect

NOTE: This function is called every frame from drawGame(), always using 
the bird's CURRENT birdY position but a FIXED X position of 10.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.4 void updateGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: The core game logic function. Handles physics, input, pipe 
movement, coin logic, animation timing, and collision detection. Called 
once per frame from loop().

SECTION-BY-SECTION BREAKDOWN:

  A) BIRD MOVEMENT (Physics)
     - Reads button state; if pressed, sets velocity = jump (-4), giving 
       an instant upward impulse
     - Adds gravity (+1) to velocity every frame regardless of input 
       (simulates constant downward pull)
     - Updates birdY by adding velocity (birdY += velocity)
     
     RESULT: Pressing the button repeatedly keeps the bird aloft; 
     releasing it causes the bird to fall due to accumulating gravity.

  B) PIPE MOVEMENT & MOVING GAPS (for-loop over 3 pipes)
     - Each pipe moves left by 'speed' pixels per frame (pipeX[i] -= speed)
     - Each pipe's gap position oscillates up/down by pipeDir[i] pixels 
       per frame, bouncing between Y=10 and Y=44 (this creates the 
       "moving gap" difficulty twist not found in the original Flappy Bird)
     - When a pipe moves fully off-screen (pipeX[i] < -10):
         - It resets to X=128 (right edge, off-screen)
         - Gets a new random gap position and direction
         - Score increments by 1
         - Every 5 points: level increases, speed increases, and 
           gapHeight decreases (down to a minimum of 10px) - this is 
           the PROGRESSIVE DIFFICULTY system

  C) BONUS COIN LOGIC
     - Each frame, if no coin is currently active, there's a 2% random 
       chance a new coin spawns at the right edge (X=128) with a random 
       Y position between 10-54
     - Active coins move left at the same speed as pipes
     - If a coin moves off the left edge (X < -5), it deactivates
     - Collision check: if the coin is within 5px (both X and Y) of the 
       bird's position, the coin is collected: +3 score, coin deactivates

  D) BIRD ANIMATION TIMING
     - Uses millis() (not delay()) to toggle flapFrame every 100ms
     - This non-blocking timing technique allows animation to update 
       independently of the main game loop's delay(30), keeping wing 
       flap speed consistent regardless of game speed changes

  E) COLLISION DETECTION
     - For each of the 3 pipes: if the pipe is horizontally aligned with 
       the bird (pipeX[i] between 0 and 14, since bird is at X=10 with 
       some width) AND the bird's Y position is outside the gap 
       (birdY < gapYArr[i] OR birdY > gapYArr[i] + gapHeight), then 
       gameOver = true
     - Additionally, if the bird goes above the screen (birdY < 0) or 
       below the screen (birdY > 64), gameOver = true (prevents bird 
       from flying off-screen indefinitely)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.5 void drawGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Renders the current frame to the OLED display. Called once per 
frame from loop(), immediately after updateGame().

DRAWING ORDER:
  1. Clear the display buffer (display.clearDisplay())
  2. Draw the bird at fixed X=10, current birdY (calls drawBird())
  3. Draw all 3 pipes:
     - Top portion: filled rectangle from Y=0 to Y=gapYArr[i]
     - Bottom portion: filled rectangle from Y=(gapYArr[i]+gapHeight) 
       to Y=64
     - This creates the "gap" visual effect - two solid blocks with an 
       empty space between them
  4. Draw the bonus coin (if active) as a hollow circle
  5. Draw HUD text:
     - "S:" (Score) at top-right area, position (90, 0)
     - "L:" (Level) below it, position (90, 10)
  6. Push everything to the physical screen (display.display())

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.6 void drawStartScreen()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Displays the title screen shown before the game begins.

CONTENT SHOWN:
  - "FLAPPY BIRD" title text at (30, 20)
  - "Press Button to" instruction at (20, 40)
  - "Start" at (45, 50)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.7 void drawGameOver()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Displays the game over screen after a collision.

CONTENT SHOWN:
  - "GAME OVER" text at (30, 20)
  - "Score: [final score]" at (30, 40)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.8 void resetGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Resets all game variables to their initial state, allowing the 
player to start a new game after Game Over.

RESET ACTIONS:
  - birdY back to 32 (center)
  - velocity back to 0
  - score back to 0
  - level back to 1
  - speed back to 2
  - gapHeight back to 20 (undoes difficulty progression)
  - gameOver set to false
  - gameStarted set to false (returns to start screen, not directly 
    into gameplay)
  - All 3 pipes re-initialized with fresh positions and random gaps
  - coinActive set to false

