7. KEY TECHNICAL CONCEPTS DEMONSTRATED
================================================================================

1. GAME LOOP PATTERN
   Clear -> Update -> Draw -> Display -> Delay (repeated every frame)

2. NON-BLOCKING ANIMATION TIMING
   Using millis() instead of delay() for the wing-flap animation allows 
   it to run independently of the main loop's frame delay.

3. ARRAY-BASED OBJECT MANAGEMENT
   Managing 3 pipes simultaneously using arrays (pipeX[], gapYArr[], 
   pipeDir[]) instead of writing repetitive code for each pipe.

4. PROCEDURAL SPRITE DRAWING
   The bird is not an image/bitmap - it's built from primitive shapes 
   (circle + triangle + circle) layered together, including using 
   BLACK color to create a "cutout" eye effect.

5. PROGRESSIVE DIFFICULTY SCALING
   Speed increases and gap size decreases automatically as the score 
   milestone (every 5 points) is reached, keeping the game engaging.

6. BASIC AABB (Axis-Aligned Bounding Box) COLLISION DETECTION
   Simplified collision logic checking X-range overlap and Y-range 
   validity for pipe collisions.

7. STATE MACHINE ARCHITECTURE
   Three distinct states (Start Screen, Playing, Game Over) controlled 
   by boolean flags (gameStarted, gameOver), managed centrally in loop().

