9. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE: Button doesn't respond / bird doesn't jump
FIX: Check the digitalRead(buttonPin) == HIGH comparisons throughout the 
     code. If your button is wired as Normally Open with INPUT_PULLUP, 
     a press typically reads LOW, not HIGH. Change all instances of 
     "== HIGH" to "== LOW" for button detection (comments in the code 
     mark exactly where these checks occur).

ISSUE: Display shows nothing / blank screen
FIX: Verify all SPI pin connections match the #define statements at the 
     top of the code. Also confirm display.begin(0, true) executes 
     without error - try adding Serial.print() debug statements if unsure.

ISSUE: Bird immediately falls through screen at start
FIX: Check that birdY is initialized to 32 and gravity/jump values are 
     reasonable (gravity should be small, e.g., 1; jump should be a 
     larger negative number, e.g., -4 to -8).

ISSUE: Game runs too fast/slow
FIX: Adjust the delay(30) value in the loop() function - increase for 
     slower gameplay, decrease for faster gameplay.

ISSUE: Random pipe patterns are identical every power-on
FIX: Ensure randomSeed(analogRead(0)) in setup() is reading from an 
     unconnected analog pin (floating pin gives better randomness). If 
     A0 is connected to something, try a different unused analog pin.

